\ cv8b-knumber.4 - NUMBER? in one dispatch (Iteration 295), for the
\ byte-header system with klookup; loaded after cv8b-klookup.4 for designs
\ with the gene knumber. X8 words: the kernel's word gets the body.
\
\ On seed 49's fastest designs NUMBER?'s own Forth, around (>NUMBER) - an
\ opcode since Iteration 57 - was 10-13% of the corpus's dispatches
\ (lab/evolve/word-cost.py). (NUMBER?) is NUMBER? with BASE @ and DPL
\ given, for the opcode; its Forth body is the kernel's NUMBER?, step for
\ step, reading BASE and DPL itself - but for its two failure paths, which
\ leave 0 0 0, where the kernel's left c-addr u 0 or ud c-addr u 0:
\ NUMBER?'s one caller, INTERPRET, aborts or throws on the 0, and a
\ throw's CATCH restores the stack's depth, so no caller sees which.

: (NUMBER?) ( c-addr base dpl --- d f )
  2DROP
  DUP C@ 3 = IF DUP 1+ C@ 39 = OVER 3 + C@ 39 = AND IF -1 DPL ! 2 + C@ 0 -1 EXIT THEN THEN
  -1 DPL !
  BASE @ >R
  COUNT
  OVER C@ 45 = DUP >R IF    -1 + SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN
  OVER C@ 36 = IF 16 BASE ! -1 + SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN
  OVER C@ 35 = IF 10 BASE ! -1 + SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN
  OVER C@ 37 = IF  2 BASE ! -1 + SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN
  R@ 0= IF OVER C@ 45 = IF R> DROP -1 >R -1 + SWAP 1 + SWAP THEN THEN
  DUP  0 > 0= IF  2DROP R> DROP R> BASE ! 0 0 0 EXIT THEN
  >R >R 0 0 R> R>
  BEGIN
   >NUMBER
   DUP IF OVER C@ 46 = IF -1 + DUP DPL ! SWAP 1 + SWAP ELSE
         2DROP 2DROP R> DROP R> BASE ! 0 0 0 EXIT THEN
       THEN
  DUP 0= UNTIL 2DROP R> IF DNEGATE THEN
  R> BASE ! -1 ;

: NUMBER?8 ( c-addr --- d f )
  BASE @ DPL (NUMBER?) ;
